{"reference":"Joel 3","book":"Joel","chapter":3,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"chapter_overview","title":"Overview","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Joel 3 presents a judgment scene in which the nations are called to account for scattering Judah and Jerusalem, dividing land, trafficking people, taking valuables, and shedding innocent blood. The chapter moves from these accusations to a vision of judgment, refuge for God’s people, and enduring fertility and security for Judah and Jerusalem.","verse_refs":["Joel 3:1-5","Joel 3:1-8","Joel 3:18-21","Joel 3:9-21"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_joel_003_33e593cb0c60eb40bad01031"]}]},{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Reading the Judgment Imagery","blocks":[{"id":"block_2","text":"The valley of Jehoshaphat and the “valley of decision” function as scenes of divine judgment. Their precise geographical location is uncertain, so the chapter’s emphasis falls on the judgment imagery rather than on identifying a modern place. The named regions and peoples belong to the book’s rhetoric and possible historical memories; they should not be turned into stereotypes of living peoples.","verse_refs":["Joel 3:1-17","Joel 3:1-21","Joel 3:1-8","Joel 3:18-21"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_joel_003_7e42d727457a620d4c55d7bd"]},{"id":"block_3","text":"Chapter numbering can cause confusion: the Masoretic form of Joel commonly has four chapters, while many English Bibles have three. Thus references to Joel 3 in a four-chapter numbering system may correspond to Joel 2:28–32 in common English numbering; this chapter is the final chapter in the three-chapter arrangement.","verse_refs":["Joel 3:1-5","Joel 3:1-8","Joel 3:18-21","Joel 3:9-21"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_joel_003_33e593cb0c60eb40bad01031"]}]},{"kind":"cultural_context","title":"A Necessary Caution","blocks":[{"id":"block_4","text":"The chapter’s martial and judgment language does not authorize readers to enact vengeance, target ethnic or religious groups, wage holy war, commit genocide, or treat human violence as divine permission.","verse_refs":["Joel 3:1-21"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_joel_003_5b41ba2188ee39e1e1a5b448"]}]}],"generated_metadata":null}